TUC Next
========

Based on Trust User Certificates by lupohan44:
https://github.com/lupohan44/TrustUserCertificates

Modified by kiber.io on 2026-10-15. This fork adds per-app and global
certificate policies, System/User/Both modes, work-profile and secondary-user
support, Zygisk integration, and a Material 3 KernelSU WebUI.
This is a modified fork, not an official release by the original author.

Further modified by kiber.io on 2026-10-19 to support User/Both injection in
profiles with an uninitialized user CA directory, without installing CA files
into Android's real store.

Further modified by kiber.io on 2026-10-22 to add optional per-app CT, system CA and user
CA trust hooks through Android's Network Security Configuration.

The project as a whole is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public
License, version 3. See LICENSE for the complete terms, including the
disclaimer of warranty and the rights to modify and redistribute the work.

Corresponding source and build instructions:
https://github.com/kiber-io/TrustUserCertificates-Next
Binary releases are accompanied by a matching tuc-next-VERSION-source.zip
in the same release. Distributors must make that corresponding source
available alongside the binary at no additional charge.

The original project's README credits HTTP Toolkit for its main logic:
https://httptoolkit.com/blog/android-14-install-system-ca-certificate/

